tags: $:/tags/Stylesheet
title: $:/Lithic/Patches/Whiteboard/PageMenuOverflow
type: text/css

/* Keep tldraw menus inside the viewport when they contain many items. The
   stock bundle hardcodes max-height: 100vh on menu panels, which are anchored
   below their trigger - so on the full-screen whiteboard layout a panel
   extends past the bottom of the screen and the last item ("Create page")
   can never be scrolled into view. Radix already computes the true available
   space and exposes it as CSS vars; use those instead of the hardcoded 100vh.
   The dropdown var covers the page select/zoom/style menus; the context-menu
   var covers right-click menus (opened at the cursor). Both fall back to the
   stock 100vh when absent, so nothing else is affected. */

.tw-whiteboard-tldraw-container [role="menu"] {
    max-height: var(
        --radix-dropdown-menu-content-available-height,
        var(--radix-context-menu-content-available-height, 100vh)
    ) !important;
}